<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nagato Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nagato Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> at the western tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>, now the western part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamaguchi-prefecture">Yamaguchi Prefecture</a>, including the strait port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimonoseki">Shimonoseki</a>. It was held by the Ōuchi and then the Mōri, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/choshu-domain">Chōshū Domain</a> combined Nagato with neighbouring Suō under the Tokugawa. The name Chōshū comes from an alternative reading of Nagato.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nagato-province.jpg" alt="Nagato Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Nagato.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
